I would spend one each on Frosty and the stack of daggers.

Ranger skill slots -

3 spell schools to maximum costs 6 slots in the late game
29 - 6 = 23 slots.

Daggers to Expert 6 slots 23 - 6 = 17 slots.

Long sword and broadsword for melee to Basic, Frosty and
Stormy 2 slots 17 - 2 = 15 slots.

Since bow and crossbow each cost 6 slots each you could
eventually move them both to Expert 12 slots.  17 - 12 = 5
slots to spare.

Those 5 slots could be spent on 3 to get polearms to Skilled
leaving you 2 slots for random enhancement.

Dagger and crossbow in the early game, melee weapons
next, bow as you approach the Quest, spells after getting
bow up to Expert.

In most ranger games it would be more like dagger to Expert
in the early game plus darts to Basic thanks to kind gnomes
leaving you stacks of them.  Then bow toward Expert once
centaurs start leaving you stacks as well as #untrap.  Mix
a couple of slots on melee weapons as appropriate before
facing Medusa.  With spells advanced in the late game if
you go to XP=30.

Rangers are based on LoTR Aragorn son of Arathron.  Melee
weapons of broadsword and longsword make sense.  For a
chaotic maybe even name Orcrist in anticipation of Stormy.



